Expected elements: present

All four changes touching this view landed. `AGE / No timestamp published` (y≈1008) and `TYPE / public` (y≈970) are labelled grid rows; the full hash sits in a bordered raised box at (506–921, y≈278–309) with a `click to select` caption at x≈934 — a resting affordance, not a hover one. The provenance note now spans the grid flush-left from x≈528 (was flush-right at ~28ch), `COST · MANA 42000 / 100000 mana (FeeJuice)` is base ten, the decoded-input note states the third case ("no call data accompanies it here") and so no longer promises an ABI remedy with no control — that resolves the vd8-r3 finding. Breadcrumb reads `Home / demo / tx / …` and the marker says `Synthetic demo data`, consistent, one marker only. Missing `value`/`nonce` rows are not a finding: §7.2 requires adapter rows, not an EVM template.

Density is the weak point. The 1920 viewport carries a 909px column and 2818px of scroll (2.6 screens) for 9 facts, four sentences and six lines of JSON. Every grid row is 909px wide with content ending by x≈1043 — 372px empty on all nine. Events/Internal calls/State changes spend 475px (y 1691–2166) on 46 words, one of which repeats the hero line at y≈571. Statement cards stop at x≈1202 while grids reach x≈1415, so the column has two right edges.

Fixes: pair the grid or reclaim the empty 41%; compress the three statement sections.

Rating: 6/10

